And then the whole group of 900-plus people

257
00:15:05,760 --> 00:15:08,680
who are friends of the Scoutmaster blog on Facebook

258
00:15:08,680 --> 00:15:10,480
join in.

259
00:15:10,480 --> 00:15:12,760
Andre asked this question.

260
00:15:12,760 --> 00:15:15,680
He said: OK, here's one for all of you out there.

261
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:17,760
I'm a new assistant scoutmaster,

262
00:15:17,760 --> 00:15:20,920
So you can see the question is, from that point of view,

263
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:23,680
Understanding. it is now up to the boys,

264
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:25,800
my son included, to do it for themselves.

265
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:28,160
What approach do you use to nudge them along

266
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:30,760
when they seem to stall out on a merit badge

267
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:32,560
or any other project?

268
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:35,800
My son has four badges started but does not

269
00:15:35,800 --> 00:15:37,360
seem motivated to finish them.

270
00:15:37,360 --> 00:15:39,760
What can I do to motivate him without being

271
00:15:39,760 --> 00:15:43,560
an interfering dad or an interfering Scoutmaster?

272
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:45,760
Andre, first of all, thanks for asking the question,

273
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:47,319
But that's a pretty big question.

274
00:15:47,319 --> 00:15:49,240
A lot of people join me in trying

275
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,640
to offer you some advice.

276
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:52,840
I'll begin by repeating what I had to say:

277
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:55,520
You can't stop being a Scoutmaster

278
00:15:55,520 --> 00:15:58,000
and you can't stop being a dad,

279
00:15:58,040 --> 00:16:01,240
And every single dad at times will encounter

280
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:03,120
the same frustrations you're experiencing.

281
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:05,880
I know that I did

282
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:08,520
My best. advice is: scouting is something

283
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:12,440
our sons get to do for themselves and we get to observe.

284
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:14,120
I think it's important that you understand

285
00:16:14,120 --> 00:16:18,000
it's possible that your input, however well intentioned,

286
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,800
can be interpreted by your son as being interfering.

287
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:25,920
Maybe you can put your dad hat on for a minute-

288
00:16:25,960 --> 00:16:29,840
And when I say a minute I'm kind of being literal there-

289
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:31,560
Short period of time-

290
00:16:31,560 --> 00:16:34,240
And tell him that you want to see him finish what he started

291
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:36,120
and ask him how he's going to make that happen

292
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:38,200
And if he needs any help from you,

293
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:42,120
and you may get a response there and you may not

294
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:44,320
just let him know that you're on the job.

295
00:16:44,320 --> 00:16:46,240
You can also leave it alone

296
00:16:46,240 --> 00:16:48,160
And he may finish them or he may not,

297
00:16:48,160 --> 00:16:51,000
Because in the grand scheme of things

298
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,520
this may not be a big deal.

299
00:16:52,520 --> 00:16:55,600
A lot of Scouts begin merit badges and don't finish them

300
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:57,840
because they find out that they're not all that interested

301
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:58,680
in the merit badge

302
00:16:58,680 --> 00:17:01,360
And I really don't have a problem with that.

303
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:03,320
I'd rather they move on to something else

304
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:05,400
that really interests them.

305
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:09,520
Another thing you can do is ask another assistant scout master

306
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:12,240
or the scout master or another adult leader

307
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:15,160
within your troop to kind of follow up with your son

308
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:19,079
on that and offer to do the same for his son,

309
00:17:19,079 --> 00:17:21,760
And that way you have a little plausible deniability

310
00:17:21,760 --> 00:17:24,680
about your scheme, although the boys usually managed

311
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:26,600
to figure that out pretty quickly.

312
00:17:26,600 --> 00:17:29,600
There's a whole thicket of issues between dads and sons

313
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:32,560
in scouting and in sports and so on,

314
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:35,200
But there are great opportunities to work things out together

315
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:36,680
and to watch them grow.

316
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:40,800
Sometimes our job is to be that dissatisfied parent

317
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:42,360
and to challenge them,

318
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:46,600
And sometimes our job is to step back and watch.

319
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:49,240
And it's really difficult to know what to do

320
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:50,880
in any given situation.

321
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:52,920
And I want to hasten to add

322
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:55,360
this is the same thing.

323
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:56,880
Being a mom is different, yes,

324
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:59,520
but the same advice applies when it comes

325
00:17:59,520 --> 00:18:02,320
to the relationship you have with your son in scouting.

326
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:04,480
If you think you're gonna interfere in the situation,

327
00:18:04,480 --> 00:18:07,160
trust your instincts and leave it be.

328
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:09,120
Mike Mansor joined in the conversation

329
00:18:09,120 --> 00:18:11,880
and he said I followed my two boys through Cubs

330
00:18:11,880 --> 00:18:13,360
and now into Boy Scouts.

331
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:16,760
I was always a den leader and now I'm their scout master.

332
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:20,720
I'm not sure who this is the hardest on- me or them.

333
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:23,440
My oldest is now our senior patrol leader.

334
00:18:23,440 --> 00:18:25,000
Try that on for difficulty.

335
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,520
Yeah, been there, done that, Mike.

336
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:30,200
In the end I think you have to let them go

337
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:31,480
at their own pace.

338
00:18:31,480 --> 00:18:32,840
That's good advice, Mike.

339
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:35,400
Sharon Miller said: definitely nudge.

340
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:39,680
I can only assume that your son is maybe 11 or 12

341
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:43,120
and mom probably still has to remind him to take a shower.

342
00:18:46,180 --> 00:18:49,760
So nudging is, you know, it's very parental,

343
00:18:49,760 --> 00:18:50,920
It's very proper,

344
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:52,360
It's what you do.

345
00:18:52,360 --> 00:18:53,920
Randall Cox said: keep it fun.

346
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:55,960
His friends should be there.

347
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:58,160
Competition with them will be a motivator

348
00:18:58,160 --> 00:18:59,560
for the first few years.

349
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:01,360
Well, that's true too.

350
00:19:01,360 --> 00:19:04,760
You know, the other scouts will probably do a better job

351
00:19:04,760 --> 00:19:06,800
of motivating him than you will.

352
00:19:06,800 --> 00:19:08,520
And then again there are guys that just don't care

353
00:19:08,520 --> 00:19:09,520
what anybody else has.

354
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:10,920
They kind of make up their own minds

355
00:19:10,920 --> 00:19:14,260
and they decide they're gonna finish something or not,

356
00:19:14,260 --> 00:19:18,200
And I think that is equally laudable.

357
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:21,640
But thanks, Randall, for joining in the conversation.

358
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:25,440
Farrell Gilmer said: there's not a lot you can do

359
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:28,120
for the other boys without their parents being involved

360
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:29,560
in their scouting career.

361
00:19:29,560 --> 00:19:32,240
Some boys are more motivated than others

362
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:34,320
And you can mention over and over to some

363
00:19:34,320 --> 00:19:37,600
that they have quite a few requirements to finish.

364
00:19:37,600 --> 00:19:40,040
But besides that, if their parents aren't helping

365
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:42,880
or pushing their son, there's not a whole lot you can do

366
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:45,840
For your own son. have them set a goal for each badge.

367
00:19:45,879 --> 00:19:49,480
My son set a goal to get Eagle before he turned 15..

368
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:51,439
In order to motivate him, I would find him

369
00:19:51,439 --> 00:19:53,600
playing his video game and would say:

370
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:55,520
you know, you have to work on this merit badge.

371
00:19:55,520 --> 00:19:56,679
He would say yes,

372
00:19:56,679 --> 00:19:58,840
And I would ask him when he was going to work on it.

373
00:19:58,840 --> 00:20:01,080
He generally said that he would get to it

374
00:20:01,080 --> 00:20:04,800
and I would then reply: what was your goal? again,

375
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:07,120
As soon as I said that he would sigh, get up

376
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:09,000
and work on his requirements,

377
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:12,760
He got his Eagle one month before he turned 15..

378
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:15,040
Farrell- that's a good story,

379
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:16,120
I like that-

380
00:20:16,120 --> 00:20:19,440
Didn't get his Eagle six months before he turned 15..

381
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:26,159
But again on the theme, sometimes that parental nudge

382
00:20:26,159 --> 00:20:29,040
is the only appropriate action to have

383
00:20:29,040 --> 00:20:30,639
And I like what Farrell did there.

384
00:20:30,639 --> 00:20:32,360
Well, tell me what your goal was again,

385
00:20:32,360 --> 00:20:35,200
Remind me what you committed yourself to,

386
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:39,680
And that's done pretty non-judgmentally

387
00:20:39,680 --> 00:20:42,440
and it's done in a spirit of fairness

388
00:20:42,440 --> 00:20:46,920
And I really like the balance of that particular statement.

389
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:48,480
Finally, Andre Crawford said

390
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:51,000
thanks to everyone for the comments.

391
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,920
So far I've been taking the hands-off approach

392
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:56,960
and only asking my son how it's going every eight

393
00:20:56,960 --> 00:20:58,040
to 10 days.

394
00:20:58,040 --> 00:20:59,880
I don't want to interfere

395
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:02,920
but I don't want to see him fail either.

396
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:04,840
It's a fine line. I'm learning to walk

397
00:21:04,840 --> 00:21:07,800
And you know, Andre, it's a fine line

398
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:11,080
that we all go through. we all work with.

399
00:21:11,080 --> 00:21:12,760
It's frustrating at times.

400
00:21:12,760 --> 00:21:16,840
It is difficult to know what to do, what not to do

401
00:21:16,840 --> 00:21:20,960
And, let's face it, we're gonna make mistakes as we go along.

402
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:23,800
But be patient with yourself, be patient with your son

403
00:21:23,800 --> 00:21:28,800
And remember that you are having one rare experience

404
00:21:28,800 --> 00:21:29,760
in today's world:

405
00:21:29,760 --> 00:21:32,560
You are working right along with him,

406
00:21:32,560 --> 00:21:35,840
watching and observing and seeing him grow up

407
00:21:35,840 --> 00:21:38,000
in a way that a lot of parents don't get

408
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:39,360
get the chance to see.

409
